sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a cylinder is cut by a plane parallel to its opposite planes, then the cylinder is to the cylinder as the axis is to the axis.
----
proof:

Let the cylinder {AD} be cut by the plane {GH} parallel to the opposite planes {AB} and {CD}. Let the plane {GH} meet the axis at the point {K}.

I say that the cylinder {BG} is to the cylinder {GD} as the axis {EK} is to the axis {KF}.

Produce the axis {EF} in both directions to the points {L} and {M}. Set out any number whatever of axes {EN} and {NL} equal to the axis {EK}, and any number whatever {FO} and {OM} equal to {FK|KF}. Construct the cylinder {PW} on the axis {LM} with the circles {PQ|Lcirc} and {VW|Mcirc} as bases.

<center>
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="540" height="210" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.13 diagram" src="propXII13.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Equimultiples of the axis EK and the cylinder BG, of the axis KF and
    // the cylinder GD: LK is as many times EK as QG is of BG, KM as many
    // times KF as WG is of GD (XII.11, the bases being equal), and the
    // comparison of LK with KM matches that of QG with GW, so V.Def.5.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the cylinder AD cut by GH (its circles and
    // faces Ecirc, ABHG, Kcirc, GHDC, Fcirc), the axis LM, the circles at
    // L, N, O, M, and the lines PV, QW. All kept. The construction (LM,
    // the circles at L, N, O, M, PV, QW, and the points on them) is held
    // back until the proof reaches it. Solid slide twins, hidden at rest
    // (initiallyHidden): the axis EF and its productions EL, FM, which
    // stroke outward from E and F; and the edges AC, BD of the cylinder AD
    // before PV, QW are drawn. Everything else added is transparent:
    // faceless twins of the circles AB, GH, CD (the originals have opaque
    // faces, raised over the figure when lit, #140); the cylinders' axial
    // sections AD, BG, GD, PW, QR, RB, QG, WG, standing for the cylinders
    // (lit with their two base circles); and the axes EK, KF, EN, NL, FO,
    // OM, KL, KM. Draggables (checked against the bundle): E, K, F, A,
    // givens. L, M, N, O and B..W are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["Ecirc","ABHG","Kcirc","GHDC","Fcirc","AB","GH","CD",
                 "AD","BG","GD","A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","K",
                 "EF","AC","BD","EK","KF"];
    var PROD  = GIVEN.concat(["EL","FM","L","M"]);
    var SETN  = PROD.concat(["N","EN","NL"]);
    var SETO  = SETN.concat(["O","FO","OM"]);
    var CPW   = SETO.concat(["LM","Lcirc","Mcirc","PV","QW","P","Q","V","W","PW"]);
    var CRT   = CPW.concat(["Ncirc","Ocirc","R","S","T","U","QR","RB","QG","WG",
                 "KL","KM"]);
    var CYL_AD = ["AB","CD","AD"];
    var CYL_BG = ["AB","GH","BG"];
    var CYL_GD = ["GH","CD","GD"];
    var CYL_PW = ["Lcirc","Mcirc","PW"];
    var CYL_QR = ["Lcirc","Ncirc","QR"];
    var CYL_RB = ["Ncirc","AB","RB"];
    var CYL_QG = ["Lcirc","GH","QG"];
    var CYL_WG = ["GH","Mcirc","WG"];
    var BASES3 = ["Lcirc","Ncirc","AB"];
    var REST  = CRT.filter(function (n) {
        return ["EF","EL","FM","AC","BD"].indexOf(n) < 0; });
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XII.13",
        elements: [
            "E0;point;fixed;-10000,110,0",
            "E3;point;fixed;10000,110,0",
            "E;point;lineSlider;E0,E3,170,0,0",
            "U0;point;fixed;-10000,110,-4000",
            "K;point;lineSlider;U0,E,240,0,0",
            "F;point;lineSlider;U0,E,340,0,0",
            "Eplane;plane;perpendicular;E,U0;0;0;0;0",
            "Kplane;plane;perpendicular;K,U0;0;0;0;0",
            "Fplane;plane;perpendicular;F,U0;0;0;0;0",
            "A';point;perpendicular;E,E0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;E,A',0,40",
            "B;point;extend;A,E,A,E",
            "C;point;parallelogram;F,E,A",
            "D;point;parallelogram;F,E,B",
            "G;point;parallelogram;K,E,A",
            "H;point;parallelogram;K,E,B",
            "Ecirc;circle;radius;E,A,Eplane;0;0;black;160,60,100",
            "ABHG;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,H,G;0;0;0;160,60,100",
            "Kcirc;circle;radius;K,E,A,Kplane;0;0;black;20,75,90",
            "GHDC;polygon;quadrilateral;G,H,D,C;0;0;0;20,75,90",
            "Fcirc;circle;radius;F,E,A,Fplane;0;0;black;20,60,100",
            "N;point;extend;K,E,K,E",
            "L;point;extend;K,N,K,E",
            "O;point;extend;K,F,K,F",
            "M;point;extend;K,O,K,F",
            "LM;line;connect;L,M",
            "Nplane;plane;perpendicular;N,U0;0;0;0;0",
            "Lplane;plane;perpendicular;L,U0;0;0;0;0",
            "Oplane;plane;perpendicular;O,U0;0;0;0;0",
            "Mplane;plane;perpendicular;M,U0;0;0;0;0",
            "Ncirc;circle;radius;N,E,A,Nplane;0;0;black;0",
            "Lcirc;circle;radius;L,E,A,Lplane;0;0;black;0",
            "Ocirc;circle;radius;O,E,A,Oplane;0;0;black;0",
            "Mcirc;circle;radius;M,E,A,Mplane;0;0;black;0",
            "P;point;parallelogram;L,E,A",
            "Q;point;parallelogram;L,E,B",
            "R;point;parallelogram;N,E,A",
            "S;point;parallelogram;N,E,B",
            "T;point;parallelogram;O,E,A",
            "U;point;parallelogram;O,E,B",
            "V;point;parallelogram;M,E,A",
            "W;point;parallelogram;M,E,B",
            "PV;line;connect;P,V",
            "QW;line;connect;Q,W",
            // Solid slide twins, hidden at rest: the axis EF, its
            // productions, and the edges of the cylinder AD.
            "EF;line;connect;E,F",
            "EL;line;connect;E,L",
            "FM;line;connect;F,M",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            // Faceless twins of the circles AB, GH, CD.
            "AB;circle;radius;E,A,Eplane;0;0;0;0",
            "GH;circle;radius;K,E,A,Kplane;0;0;0;0",
            "CD;circle;radius;F,E,A,Fplane;0;0;0;0",
            // The cylinders' axial sections.
            "AD;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,D,C;0;0;0;0",
            "BG;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,H,G;0;0;0;0",
            "GD;polygon;quadrilateral;G,H,D,C;0;0;0;0",
            "PW;polygon;quadrilateral;P,Q,W,V;0;0;0;0",
            "QR;polygon;quadrilateral;P,Q,S,R;0;0;0;0",
            "RB;polygon;quadrilateral;R,S,B,A;0;0;0;0",
            "QG;polygon;quadrilateral;P,Q,H,G;0;0;0;0",
            "WG;polygon;quadrilateral;G,H,W,V;0;0;0;0",
            // The axes.
            "EK;line;connect;E,K;0;0;0",
            "KF;line;connect;K,F;0;0;0",
            "EN;line;connect;E,N;0;0;0",
            "NL;line;connect;N,L;0;0;0",
            "FO;line;connect;F,O;0;0;0",
            "OM;line;connect;O,M;0;0;0",
            "KL;line;connect;K,L;0;0;0",
            "KM;line;connect;K,M;0;0;0"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["EF","EL","FM","AC","BD"],
        slides: [
            { text: "“If a cylinder is cut by a plane parallel to its opposite planes,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: CYL_AD.concat(["GH"]),
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.13" }] },
            { text: "then the cylinder is to the cylinder as the axis is to the axis.”",
              highlighted: CYL_BG.concat(CYL_GD).concat(["EK","KF"]) },
            { text: "Let the cylinder {AD} be cut by the plane {GH} parallel to the opposite planes {AB} and {CD}.",
              highlighted: CYL_AD.concat(["GH"]) },
            { text: "Let the plane {GH} meet the axis at the point {K}.",
              highlighted: ["GH","EF","K"] },
            { text: "I say that the cylinder {BG} is to the cylinder {GD} as the axis {EK} is to the axis {KF}.",
              highlighted: CYL_BG.concat(CYL_GD).concat(["EK","KF"]) },
            { text: "Produce the axis {EF} in both directions to the points {L} and {M}.",
              visible: PROD,
              highlighted: ["EF","L","M"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "EL", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "FM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.2" }] },
            { text: "Set out any number whatever of axes {EN} and {NL} equal to the axis {EK},",
              visible: SETN,
              highlighted: ["EN","NL","EK"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "N", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and any number whatever {FO} and {OM} equal to {FK|KF}.",
              visible: SETO,
              highlighted: ["FO","OM","KF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "O", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Construct the cylinder {PW} on the axis {LM} with the circles {PQ|Lcirc} and {VW|Mcirc} as bases.",
              visible: CPW,
              highlighted: CYL_PW.concat(["LM"]),
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "Lcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "Mcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "PV", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "QW", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Carry the planes through the points {N} and {O} parallel to {AB} and {CD} and to the bases of the cylinder {PW},",
              highlighted: ["N","O","AB","CD","Lcirc","Mcirc"] },
            { text: "and let them produce the circles {RS|Ncirc} and {TU|Ocirc} about the centers {N}, {O}.",
              visible: CRT,
              highlighted: ["Ncirc","Ocirc","N","O"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "Ncirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "Ocirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } },
            { text: "Then, since the axes {LN|NL}, {NE|EN}, and {EK} equal one another,",
              highlighted: ["NL","EN","EK"] },
            { text: "therefore the cylinders {QR}, {RB}, and {BG} are to one another as their bases.",
              highlighted: CYL_QR.concat(CYL_RB).concat(CYL_BG),
              justifications: [{ claim: "same height: as their bases", ref: "XII.11" }] },
            { text: "But the bases are equal, therefore the cylinders {QR}, {RB}, and {BG} also equal one another.",
              highlighted: CYL_QR.concat(CYL_RB).concat(CYL_BG) },
            { text: "Since then the axes {LN|NL}, {NE|EN}, and {EK} equal one another,",
              highlighted: ["NL","EN","EK"] },
            { text: "and the cylinders {QR}, {RB}, and {BG} also equal one another,",
              highlighted: CYL_QR.concat(CYL_RB).concat(CYL_BG) },
            { text: "and the multitude of the former equals the multitude of the latter,",
              highlighted: ["NL","EN","EK"].concat(BASES3).concat(["GH"]) },
            { text: "therefore, the multiple the axis {KL} is of the axis {EK}",
              highlighted: ["KL","EK"] },
            { text: "is the same multiple the cylinder {QG} is of the cylinder {GB|BG}.",
              highlighted: CYL_QG.concat(CYL_BG) },
            { text: "For the same reason, the multiple the axis {MK|KM} is of the axis {KF}",
              highlighted: ["KM","KF"] },
            { text: "is the same multiple the cylinder {WG} is of the cylinder {GD}.",
              highlighted: CYL_WG.concat(CYL_GD) },
            { text: "And, if the axis {KL} equals the axis {KM}, then the cylinder {QG} also equals the cylinder {GW|WG};",
              highlighted: ["KL","KM"].concat(CYL_QG).concat(CYL_WG) },
            { text: "if the axis is greater than the axis, then the cylinder is also greater than the cylinder; and if less, less.",
              highlighted: ["KL","KM"].concat(CYL_QG).concat(CYL_WG) },
            { text: "Thus, there being four magnitudes, the axes {EK} and {KF} and the cylinders {BG} and {GD},",
              highlighted: ["EK","KF"].concat(CYL_BG).concat(CYL_GD) },
            { text: "there have been taken equimultiples of the axis {EK} and of the cylinder {BG},",
              highlighted: ["EK"].concat(CYL_BG) },
            { text: "namely the axis {LK|KL} and the cylinder {QG},",
              highlighted: ["KL"].concat(CYL_QG) },
            { text: "and equimultiples of the axis {KF} and of the cylinder {GD},",
              highlighted: ["KF"].concat(CYL_GD) },
            { text: "namely the axis {KM} and the cylinder {GW|WG},",
              highlighted: ["KM"].concat(CYL_WG) },
            { text: "and it has been proved that, if the axis {KL} is in excess of the axis {KM},",
              highlighted: ["KL","KM"] },
            { text: "the cylinder {QG} is also in excess of the cylinder {GW|WG}; if equal, equal; and if less, less.",
              highlighted: CYL_QG.concat(CYL_WG) },
            { text: "Therefore the axis {EK} is to the axis {KF} as the cylinder {BG} is to the cylinder {GD}.",
              highlighted: ["EK","KF"].concat(CYL_BG).concat(CYL_GD),
              justifications: [{ claim: "equimultiples", ref: "V.Def.5" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, if a cylinder is cut by a plane parallel to its opposite planes,",
              visible: REST,
              highlighted: CYL_AD.concat(["GH"]) },
            { text: "then the cylinder is to the cylinder as the axis is to the axis.",
              highlighted: CYL_BG.concat(CYL_GD).concat(["EK","KF"]),
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XII.13") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.2":  "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post2/",
        "V.Def.5":   "/elements/books/bookV/definitions/defV5/",
        "XII.11":    "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII11/"
    });
</script>
</center>

Carry the planes through the points {N} and {O} parallel to {AB} and {CD} and to the bases of the cylinder {PW}, and let them produce the circles {RS|Ncirc} and {TU|Ocirc} about the centers {N}, {O}.

Then, since the axes {LN|NL}, {NE|EN}, and {EK} equal one another, therefore the cylinders {QR}, {RB}, and {BG} are to one another as their bases. [!just XII.11]

But the bases are equal, therefore the cylinders {QR}, {RB}, and {BG} also equal one another.

Since then the axes {LN|NL}, {NE|EN}, and {EK} equal one another, and the cylinders {QR}, {RB}, and {BG} also equal one another, and the multitude of the former equals the multitude of the latter, therefore, the multiple the axis {KL} is of the axis {EK} is the same multiple the cylinder {QG} is of the cylinder {GB|BG}.

For the same reason, the multiple the axis {MK|KM} is of the axis {KF} is the same multiple the cylinder {WG} is of the cylinder {GD}.

And, if the axis {KL} equals the axis {KM}, then the cylinder {QG} also equals the cylinder {GW|WG}; if the axis is greater than the axis, then the cylinder is also greater than the cylinder; and if less, less. Thus, there being four magnitudes, the axes {EK} and {KF} and the cylinders {BG} and {GD}, there have been taken equimultiples of the axis {EK} and of the cylinder {BG}, namely the axis {LK|KL} and the cylinder {QG}, and equimultiples of the axis {KF} and of the cylinder {GD}, namely the axis {KM} and the cylinder {GW|WG}, and it has been proved that, if the axis {KL} is in excess of the axis {KM}, the cylinder {QG} is also in excess of the cylinder {GW|WG}; if equal, equal; and if less, less. Therefore the axis {EK} is to the axis {KF} as the cylinder {BG} is to the cylinder {GD}. [!just V.Def.5]

Therefore, *if a cylinder is cut by a plane parallel to its opposite planes, then the cylinder is to the cylinder as the axis is to the axis.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition is preliminary to the next in which it is shown that cylinders on equal bases are proportional to their heights. It is also used in the proposition following that.
